Fresh-eyes review complete on `src/blog/people/drafts/Ibai-Llanos.md` — notes appended as a `FRESH EYES REVIEW (2026-07-30)` comment block at the bottom of the file. No body edits made.

The two biggest issues I flagged:

1. **The 2019–2020 career bridge is missing entirely.** The draft jumps from his 2018 caster wages straight to "newly independent" in February 2021, skipping the G2 Esports chapter and — more importantly — the March 2020 lockdown streams that turned him from an esports caster into Spain's national companion. That's the inflection any reader who knows Ibai will look for, and it also reframes the Piqué DM scene (Piqué was "already following" a lockdown-famous star, not a stranger). I checked the pipeline's own transcripts and logs: that era was never researched, so this is a genuine blind spot rather than a deliberate cut. The New Year's Eve campanadas streams belong to the same missing layer.

2. **The strongest belonging evidence never made it into the body.** The working notes list "lived with eight friends after getting rich" as core Type 9 evidence, but the shared house appears nowhere in the article — and Ander Cortés, introduced twice as the founding friendship, simply vanishes after the 2014 audition. For a piece whose thesis is belonging-over-everything, those are the receipts.

Secondary notes: the anger-paid-with-food thesis is pre-stated three times before the body earns it, the ledger/invoice metaphor runs four to five times and reads as a tic by the ending, and the piece could use one moment of Ibai actually being funny — he reads more solemn on the page than he ever is on camera. I also flagged what to preserve: the CPAP-as-comfort insight (the best single Enneagram read in the draft), the skeptic-then-answer structure of the Agüero section, and the bespoke wage ledger and ending.
